## 6. Production (0-25 points)

Analyze the `work`, `internship`, and `volunteer` sections. Score 18-25 for a
real internship, paid work, or substantial volunteer role directly relevant to
software engineering with evidence of meaningful contribution (not just
attendance); 9-17 for part-time/short-term experience with some technical
relevance, or unrelated work that still demonstrates professionalism and
reliability; 1-8 for minimal or tangential experience with little demonstrable
relevance.

**If `work`, `internship`, and `volunteer` are all empty or absent**, score 0
and state in evidence: "No work, internship, or volunteer experience
disclosed." This is expected and normal for an entry-level/intern candidate — it
must not be treated as a red flag beyond the raw 0 score, and must not silently
reduce the candidate's standing in any other category.

---

## 7. Technical Skills (0-15 points)

Full-stack breadth matters for this role. Score 11-15 for demonstrated breadth
across frontend, backend, and data/infrastructure layers, evidenced in projects
or work — not just a bare skills list; 6-10 for solid skills concentrated in one
or two layers of the stack; 1-5 for a narrow, generic, or unverified skill
listing with little supporting evidence elsewhere in the resume; 0 for no
meaningful technical skills evidence.

---

## 8. Bonus Points (maximum 20 points total, stated here only)

+2 for a personal portfolio/website URL in `basics.url`. +1 for a GitHub profile
URL, only if distinct from the portfolio link above. +1 for a LinkedIn profile.
+2 to +3 for early-stage engineer experience (first 10-20 employees at a
startup). +1 to +3 for high-quality technical blogs, if blog data is provided —
regular posting, diverse technical topics.

Do NOT award bonus points for participation in competitive open-source
fellowship programs (Google Summer of Code, Outreachy, Girl Script Summer of
Code, Season of Docs). These are themselves selective admissions processes and
would reintroduce the access bias this rubric is designed to avoid.

This 20-point cap is absolute, regardless of how many of the above are
satisfied.

